+---
+id: dl-006-createpatch-minimal-structural-diff-lcs-on-arrays-no-move-or-copy-jsondifferror
+type: decision-log
+title: "createPatch: minimal structural diff, LCS on arrays, no move or copy, JsonDiffError"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# createPatch: minimal structural diff, LCS on arrays, no move or copy, JsonDiffError
+
+## Context
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document, as a JSON Patch
+(RFC 6902), produced by `createPatch(from, to)` (task-005). RFC 6902 defines how to apply a patch, not
+how to compute one, and many patches turn `from` into `to`; the request rules out any that resends
+more than what changed. Inputs may come from clients, so they are untrusted. `applyPatch` and
+`applyMergePatch` already validate JSON values through `json-value.ts` (dl-004, dl-005, pending).
+
+## Decision
+
+- Recursive structural diff: equal values give nothing (objects compared with members in any order);
+  objects are diffed member by member (`remove` for members only in `from`, in `from`'s order, then
+  `add` for members only in `to`, in `to`'s order); any other difference, including a change of type,
+  is a `replace` of that value (path `""` for the root).
+- Arrays: elements are compared through a canonical text (sorted members), the common start and end
+  are kept, and the middle is aligned on a longest common subsequence (dynamic programming). Between
+  two kept elements, removed and inserted elements are paired in order and diffed in place; the extra
+  ones are removed or added. Indexes are numeric, computed against the array as patched so far.
+- Bound on cost: when the middle parts' sizes multiply to more than 4 000 000 cells, alignment is
+  skipped and elements are compared position by position. The patch stays correct, only larger.
+- Only `add`, `remove` and `replace` are generated; no `move`, `copy` or `test`.
+- Both inputs are validated and deep-copied with `cloneJson`; patch values come from the copy of `to`.
+- Every failure throws a `JsonDiffError` (new export) whose `cause` is the underlying error; no other
+  error escapes, even from a getter or a stack overflow.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Small changes give small patches: one changed leaf is one `replace`, one inserted array element is
+  one `add`, whatever the document size.
+- Cost: O(size) to copy and canonicalize, plus O(n·m) time and 4 bytes per cell of memory for the
+  middle of each changed array, at most 16 MB per array thanks to the bound; an untrusted pair of huge
+  arrays cannot exhaust memory, but may get a positional patch.
+- The patch is not guaranteed to be the smallest possible: a moved element is a `remove` plus an `add`
+  of its whole value, and an element changed beyond recognition may be diffed in place rather than
+  replaced. Adding `move` detection later would not change the output format.
+- Generation is deterministic: the same inputs always give the same patch.
+- `JsonDiffError` is now public API and must stay stable.
