+
+# Implement RFC 6902 JSON Patch generation createPatch
+
+## Request
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document. Export
+`createPatch(from, to)` from `src/index.ts`, returning a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from` into
+`to` when applied, without mutating either input. The patch must describe what changed and nothing
+more: a small change must not resend the whole document.
+
+## Done
+
+- `src/create-patch.ts`: `createPatch` and `JsonDiffError`, both exported from `src/index.ts`. Both
+  inputs are validated and copied with `cloneJson` (`json-value.ts`), then diffed recursively: objects
+  member by member, arrays aligned on a longest common subsequence (after trimming their common start
+  and end), unmatched elements paired and diffed in place, the extras removed or added.
+- `test/create-patch.test.ts`: 20 tests, red first (the export did not exist): empty patch for equal
+  documents, member changes, adds and removes, a single change deep in a large document, null values,
+  type changes, root replacement, pointer escaping, array insertions/removals at the start, middle and
+  end, in-place element diffs, 300 deterministic pseudo-random round-trips through `applyPatch`, inputs
+  not modified and not shared, `__proto__`, large fully different arrays, and non-JSON or over-deep
+  inputs rejected as `JsonDiffError`. 119 tests pass.
+- `README.md`: JSON Patch generation section.
+- Decision: dl-006.
+
+## Notes
+
+- dl-003, dl-004 and dl-005 are still pending approval; dl-006 reuses the JSON value rules they describe.
+- `tsc` is not installed, so type-checking was not run; no coverage threshold is declared.
